 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them under,\nSaw the flame of Death's soul come burning\nDown from out the world-soul's burning\nAnd fallen on the Fallen world,\nLike a kindle coming upon\nA fallen world to light itself.\nHe heard that fire hear itself,\nHe saw it see its face; behold,\nAs if an hour before,\nA moment like itself within\nIts time to live and die in heaven,\nAnd here were dead therein and",
